                    <English> &gt;75% CFL or LED</English>
                    <French> &gt;75% CFL or LED</French>
                </Lighting>
                <ApplianceConsumption clothesDryer="916" clothesWasher="197" isClothesWasherEnergyStar="false" dishWasher="260" isDishWasherEnergyStar="false" refrigerator="639" range="565" />
                <HotWater areFaucetsReducedRate="false" areShowerHeadsReducedRate="false" />
            </ReducedOperatingConditions>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The chimney in the basement is allowin air to enter the house at a rapid pace. This needs to be assessed and fixed immediatly.



There is air leakage between the top of the foundation wall and the bottom plate.



Back door showing signs of leakage around the bottom of door.



Attic hatch needs a gasket/air seal to prevent air from entering through attic. 



Above grade walls have air leakage as it is leaking into house through electrical receptacles. 



 </airSeal>
                <doors>Front Door needs to be replaced</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>If renovations are made to make the house more "air tight", A HRV should be installed to ensure good air quality and proper supply and exhaust of air in and out of the home.</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>All water pipes entering and exiting the hot water tank should be insulated.



This is a great house to install a Drain Water Heat Recovery system as the bathroom drain is accessible from the basement.</HotWaterSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
